@startuml poll-failed-check
' cumin works - how cumin reads the content of one failed required check, for "request a check fix".
' Document: poll.md, the reading of the content of a failed check.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:Read the check runs of the commit,
every attempt (filter=all);
:Keep the runs of the name of the check,
and of the App of the rule;
if (a run that failed?) then (no)
  :Text: the name of the check,
  "could not read its content";
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Take the newest run that failed
(the highest id);
:Read the failure annotations of the run;
if (details_url: https://github.com,
and the path is
/<owner>/<repo>/actions/runs/<n>/job/<job id>
of this repository?) then (yes)
  :Read the end of the log of the job;
else (no)
  :Read no job log;
endif
if (a failure annotation,
or a job log?) then (yes)
  :Text: the annotations,
  then the end of the job log;
  stop
else (no)
  :Text: the name of the check,
  "could not read its content";
  stop
endif

note right
  Without filter=all, GitHub lists only
  the latest attempt of a name. A rerun
  that passed then hides the attempt
  that failed.
end note
@enduml
